crates/sky-types/tests/ui/ok_condition_warns.sky:5:6: warning: estimated condition number κ(H) ≈ 1.6e13: about 13 of 16 significant digits may be lost
  |
5 | x = H⁻¹ @ b
  |      ^^ inverting or solving with this magnifies errors by up to 1.6e13
  |     - this is a constant 10×10 matrix
  = note: κ(H) = σmax/σmin measures how much a matrix magnifies relative error: rounding error in the inputs (about 1.1e-16 for an `f64`) can change the solution of H·x = b by about κ(H) times as much, so about log10 κ = 13 of the 16 digits are lost. A well-conditioned matrix has κ near 1
  = help: rescale rows and columns so their entries are similar in size; or reformulate so the matrix is better posed (a different basis, fewer nearly dependent unknowns, or a regularized or least-squares formulation); higher-precision arithmetic (planned) buys back digits but not a better problem

